From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] make Agent Channel Priorities readable, and Save mean something

The table was correct and hard to use. Three problems, all visible in a
screenshot of a five-agent account:

1. EVERY ROW HAD AN ACTIVE SAVE BUTTON. A column of identical blue buttons
   tells an operator nothing about which rows they actually touched, and
   invites saving rows they never edited. Each row now remembers what the
   backend last returned (`saved`), and Save only appears when the row differs
   from it. A saved row shows a quiet "Saved" tick; an untouched row shows a
   dash. The wall of blue is gone and unsaved work is now the thing that stands
   out.

2. "ALSO HANDLES" WRAPPED INTO THREE RAGGED LINES, which is what made the rows
   tall and the table hard to scan. The Status column is folded into the Agent
   cell -- name and availability are one fact about the agent, and separating
   them spent a whole column of width that the five channel chips needed more.
   Chips are tighter (px-2/py-0.5, gap-1.5) with a `min-w-[15rem]` floor so
   they hold their line instead of collapsing one chip per row in a narrow
   viewport.

3. THE PRIMARY CHANNEL WAS ALSO TOGGLEABLE AS AN EXTRA. Primary is always
   first in the priority list, so a channel that is primary is implicitly
   handled; showing it selectable in both places reads as a double-count. The
   chip for the current primary is now disabled, with a title explaining why.
   No behaviour change on save -- `save()` already filtered the primary out of
   the extras, so this only stops the UI implying otherwise.

Row density drops from py-3 to py-2.5 with a hover highlight, and the Saving…
state is now visible on the button itself rather than only as a disabled
control.

Hunks are a real `git diff` against the component as extracted from the patched
upstream image. The `import` placement trap from 0062 does not apply here --
nothing new is imported.
